From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ImpulseROM <noreply@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] Disable StrongBox in DevRootKeyATCmd

Branch over both setIsStrongBoxBacked(true) calls; the builder default is false, which is
what a device without a StrongBox keymaster needs. The register holding 'true' is shared with
the setDevicePropertiesAttestationIncluded calls, so the constant is not flipped, and the
calls stay as dead code because the build's DEX-inventory guard needs every reference to
survive. Rebased onto One UI 8.5 DZF3.
---
 smali_classes6/com/android/server/DevRootKeyATCmd.smali | changed
 1 file changed

--- a/smali_classes6/com/android/server/DevRootKeyATCmd.smali
+++ b/smali_classes6/com/android/server/DevRootKeyATCmd.smali
@@ -3267,7 +3267,7 @@
     :goto_3
     const/4 v8, 0x4
 
-    if-ne v2, v8, :cond_5
+    goto :cond_5
 
     invoke-virtual {v11, v10}, Landroid/security/keystore/KeyGenParameterSpec$Builder;->setIsStrongBoxBacked(Z)Landroid/security/keystore/KeyGenParameterSpec$Builder;
 
@@ -3513,7 +3513,7 @@
     invoke-virtual {v11, v5}, Landroid/security/keystore/KeyGenParameterSpec$Builder;->setAttestationIds([I)Landroid/security/keystore/KeyGenParameterSpec$Builder;
 
     :cond_c
-    if-ne v2, v8, :cond_d
+    goto :cond_d
 
     invoke-virtual {v11, v10}, Landroid/security/keystore/KeyGenParameterSpec$Builder;->setIsStrongBoxBacked(Z)Landroid/security/keystore/KeyGenParameterSpec$Builder;
 
